> implicit x^y=y^x for y wrt x
on the curve x^y - y^x = 0, y as a function of x:
  dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = (y^x*log(y) - y*x^(y - 1))/(log(x)*x^y - x*y^(x - 1))
  holds where F_y = log(x)*x^y - x*y^(x - 1) != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)
  check: matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 4e-12)
